{"id": "EUVD-2026-101567", "enisaUuid": "8cc655ae-538f-3f24-be74-29d78a307215", "description": "Gitingest through 0.3.1 contains a symlink following vulnerability in ingest_query single-file blob ingestion that allows unauthenticated attackers to read server files by submitting symlink blob URLs. Attackers can commit a symlink to a public repository and submit its blob URL, causing the server to return any file the service user can read, up to 10 MB.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T18:47:44", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T18:17:02", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@hieuPenguinnn/gitingest-blob-symlink-arbitrary-file-read", "https://github.com/coderamp-labs/gitingest/blob/4e259a02fe72115bee538271622f1234a81c8e1a/src/gitingest/ingestion.py#L75", "https://github.com/coderamp-labs/gitingest", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/gitingest-through-0.3.1-arbitrary-file-read-via-symlink-in-blob-ingestion"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-110767", "GHSA-cgrx-q63r-jf38"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.41, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3d4944f3-6c2c-32d6-b30d-36bb40c2ac90", "product": {"name": "gitingest", "vendor": {"name": "coderamp-labs"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.3.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "b8deb298-d232-3997-8278-24125a4dd258", "vendor": {"name": "coderamp-labs"}}], "isExploited": false}